      "id": "mxdsn8c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "13.1 Introduction to Cyber Security"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Cyber Security focuses on protecting digital systems, networks, and data from unauthorized access or malicious attacks.",
        "Computer viruses and malware are harmful programs designed to compromise data integrity and system performance.",
        "Firewalls serve as network security systems that monitor and filter incoming and outgoing network traffic.",
        "Antivirus software performs key functions like scanning, identifying, quarantining, and eliminating malicious code.",
        "Phishing uses deceptive communication to steal user credentials, whereas hacking involves breaching system security controls."
      ],
      "id": "y76hwes"
    },
